A||N||3||kornholio||luggage rack removal||||1
Z||000000||kornholio||11-04-1999||05:39 PM||||Has anyone removed their luggage rack?  How do I remove the nuts with rubber washers on the decklid?  The last thing I want to do is drop one of them inside the decklid.  That rattling noise would drive me crazy!  And what do I use to fill the holes?  Fiberglass filler?  Thanks.||||reg||1
Z||000001||TOM||11-04-1999||11:18 PM||||I think they are like pull rivets. They should come out from the top when the rack is off. Fiberglass and a little bondo is good.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Standard||11-05-1999||12:37 AM||||I took my luggage rack off about 2 months ago.  Not hard at all.  Haven't gotten around to filling the holes yet, and I haven't taken off those rubber thingies, although 1 or 2 did fall off when I was taking the rack off.||||reg||1
Z||000003||trackerrrr||11-05-1999||11:07 PM||||kornholio,<BR>  Screw one of the screws back into the nut and just pull them straight up and out.  I took my rack off and repainted it a few weeks ago.  I pulled the rubber washer/nuts straight out to clean under them.  Just be careful not to rip the rubber part off or you'll be fishing the bottom part out of the decklid.  ||||reg||10
